<!-- WHAT WE LOOK FOR -->
<section class="cx-section" id="trades-criteria" style="background:var(--dark)">
  <div class="cx-container">
    <div class="r">
      <div class="cx-eyebrow">What We Look For</div>
      <h2 class="cx-h2">Three things we need<br>from every trade partner.</h2>
      <p class="cx-sub" style="max-width:540px;margin-top:16px">Simple requirements. But we hold to them on every project, and we expect you to as well.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cx-not-list stagger" style="margin-top:52px">
      <div class="cx-not-item r">
        <div class="cx-not-bad">Inconsistent quality</div>
        <div class="cx-not-good">Consistent craftmanship</div>
        <h3>Quality work, first time</h3>
        <p>Commercial interiors have to pass inspection and satisfy clients who will be in the space every day. We do not tolerate shortcuts. Work done wrong comes back out and comes back right, no exceptions.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cx-not-item r">
        <div class="cx-not-bad">Excuses when you do not show</div>
        <div class="cx-not-good">Reliable scheduling</div>
        <h3>On-site when you commit to be there</h3>
        <p>We run tight commercial schedules. If you book a date, you hold the date. If something changes, you tell us immediately so we can adjust the sequence. Surprises are not acceptable in deadline-driven construction.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cx-not-item r">
        <div class="cx-not-bad">Paperwork problems after the fact</div>
        <div class="cx-not-good">WSIB and insurance current</div>
        <h3>Current WSIB clearance and liability insurance</h3>
        <p>Every trade on a VNG project must carry current WSIB coverage and commercial general liability insurance at the limits we specify. This is non-negotiable. We verify before your crew steps on site.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

